                <pb facs="0818" n="698" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg698"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4329: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-04T13:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1922—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 4—8:05 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>193. Fengtien forces have evacuated Changhsintien position on the Peking–Hankow
                    Railway and are now retreating on Fengtai closely followed by Chihli troops.
                    Fengtien stragglers have appeared at west gates of Peking but gates closed
                    against them. Other city gates now closed also. An American with the Chihli side
                    has telephoned from Changhsintien that the Chihli troops have also prevailed at
                    Kuan and Machang and are now within 20 miles of Tientsin of which however we
                    have no confirmation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
